## SEVERITY / VERDICT
*Blocker:* a path beyond the five; a product byte (any change under `backend/**`, `static/**`, `.github/**`, `tests/**`, `Dockerfile`); `backend/validators.js` not byte-equal to main; the counts blob holding a pair other than the one `Build` measures (5155/306; either direction); a pre-existing cell red at the head with the product unchanged; a NEW CodeQL alert with security severity high+ or rule severity `error`, or a `CodeQL` check-run concluded failure; a merge-result tree other than main plus the five files; a gitleaks finding; a person name, decision-card id or secret in a message/title/body; the head moved; a test that writes to the clone's `.git/index` or leaves temporary directories behind (Check 3e). *Major (class named on the line, "NO GO 1 of 2"):* a POSITIVE new cell no mutant turns red (a survivor); a builder claim contradicted by your measurement that changes the basis (a blob, the 183 titles, 53 added, the RD-854 reading); `Build` red at the head for a reason not shown to be a base fact; the head message's arithmetic wrong. *Minor/Note:* a CONTROL cell with no killer; the PR body's Opus trailer; the branch name's `854`; a ticket key in a message; node version differing from CI; the `mergeable_state` text; the CodeQL check-run `neutral` while analyses run; the builder's "six paths" wording versus five (its FINDINGS 4); a cell the mutant killed with a different message than predicted; `--chmod` keyed as text and `.venv` not modelled (the builder's D9, deliberate, not in the tickets).
**VERDICT RULES.** GO needs every check-run at the head completed and green, all three Analyze runs complete with both thresholds met, `Build` completed green with its four verify lines quoted, Checks 1, 2, 3, 4, 6 measured with their controls. While `build` or any Analyze run is pending the verdict is at most GO WITH FINDINGS and the line above the last line names the pending set. A NO GO names the class and "round 1 of 2" and gives the fix-shape in prose. **STOP (`STOPPED: NEEDS TUESDAY <the change and why>`) if** the delta holds a path beyond the five, the head moved (C-68), main moved into the five paths or `backend/server.js`/`backend/validators.js`/`Dockerfile` (the merge ref and the counts change under you), a request leaves loopback from your own scripts (other than GitHub GETs, npm as `npm ci` itself reaches it, `git fetch`), or a security-shaped finding you cannot classify.
**First line of STATUS (the verdict line; at Step 0 the placeholder `GATE VERDICT B714: PENDING`):** `GATE VERDICT B714: pr117 <GO|GO WITH FINDINGS|NO GO> @ f1d23b2 (round 1 of 2 on class "a new test cell that pins less than it claims" - delta <7 commits, 5 paths, +286 -21, numstat per path y/n; blobs y/n; product bytes 0 y/n; validators blob 37ff4001 y/n> - cells <rd777 97->121, rd848 19->48, rd618 14->14, added 53, missing 0, distinct 183 y/n> - kills <positive cells killed n of n; controls killed n of n; survivors n; mutants k of m as predicted; pre-existing red 0 y/n> - gap proof <main's R8 green under C2 and C3 y/n> - env <GIT_* hook shape clean y/n; tmp leftovers 0 y/n; 3 runs flake 0 y/n> - RD-854 drop <honest|partly|not>; live cells red under the fix n - counts <5102+53=5155 y/n; counts blob fd0f3b0d y/n; Build verify lines 5155/306 y/n; own verify NOT TESTED (Q-2)> - CI <n completed success of n; pending <names|none>; failing <names|none>> - CodeQL <analyses n of 3 at the head; Analyze complete y/n; open alerts on PR ref n; new high+ n; new error n; check-run conclusion x> - merge <ahead 7 behind 0 y/n; parents main+head y/n; tree equals GitHub's y/n; main sha7 at start and end> - Deploy demo <starts, both jobs skipped y/n> - gitleaks rc <n>)`. Then the sections: Step 0 (sha256s, slot count), REFUSE counts, PINS, instrument and load, Checks 1-6 each with the FAIL clock and the evidence path, the mutant matrix and the 53-row attribution table, the builder-claims table (claim, your number, agree y/n), FOR TUESDAY (the verdict in plain words with the class and round; what stands between the PR and a landing, naming the Analyze runs and `build` if pending; the head-pinned MERGE-commit landing command above with the quoted `:2067` text, never squash, never rebase; what a merge starts: a `Deploy demo` run expected `skipped`; to read after landing: main's push `Build` and the CodeQL push analysis; the records seat moves RD-882, RD-850, RD-851, RD-852, RD-843 and the RD-854 follow-up, not the gate; the later counts lanes (RD-849, RD-878) and B713 wait on the counts file), FOUND / TESTED / HOW / NOT TESTED / corrections / processes, ports and trees left, **UNMEASURED**. **Last line, exactly one of:** `VERDICT: B714 pr117 b703/nexusai-counts-882-850-851-852-854-843 @ <sha7> <GO|GO WITH FINDINGS|NO GO> (round 1 of 2) on main <sha7>` (main by `ls-remote` at verdict; the line carries none of the words that name a landing; the findings ids with severities, classes and the CI state sit on the line above it), or `STOPPED: NEEDS TUESDAY <one question>`.
**LANDING HOLD (Tuesday's, restated by you, done by you never).** After a GO or GO WITH FINDINGS with every check-run complete at the head: Tuesday lands the SAME commit as a MERGE COMMIT, head-pinned: `gh pr merge 117 -R datasecau/Reporting_Dashboard_Au --merge --match-head-commit f1d23b25cb5eee268bcb82835200e5d5a2f7a37d` under the NexusAI `GH_CONFIG_DIR`. Never squash (C-190/C-68), never rebase, CodeQL never bypassed, no alert dismissed, the ruleset untouched. This gate does none of it.
